=== A. M is a market-center official close, not the consolidated last ===
  regular last 100.03; M official-close print 100.00
  consolidated last stays 100.03; volume stays 1,000,000
  participant last updates to 100.00
  do not use an M print as the consolidated official close, or fold it into the regular-hours last sale
=== B. Q updates the consolidated open, not the consolidated last or volume ===
  Q official-open print 50.00 -> consolidated open 50.00; consolidated last 50.10; volume 0
  participant last stays 50.10; participant high/low includes 50.00-50.10
=== C. T is not last-sale eligible; it does update volume, including ETH ===
  T print 99.50 at 21:30 ET, Extended Early Hours 21:00-09:30; size 2,000
    consolidated last stays 100.03; volume 1,000,000 -> 1,002,000
  T print 100.40 at 16:15 ET, after the 16:00 close; size 3,000
    consolidated last stays 100.03; volume 1,002,000 -> 1,005,000
  CTA ETH FAQ v1.2 Q11: T applies to Extended Early Hours 21:00-09:30 and any trades after the 16:00 close
  Q12: ETH trades are included in consolidated volume; T is not Last Sale eligible
  UTP September 2026 Note 1 still lists Form T as 12:00 a.m.-9:30 a.m. and 4:00:01 p.m.-8:00 p.m.;
  that note has not been rewritten for 23/5 — do not use it to deny that overnight ETH prints are T
=== D. 6 is a closing trade, not the same flag as M ===
  condition 6 closing trade 100.02, size 10,000 -> consolidated last 100.02; volume 1,010,000
  6 updates consolidated last? True; updates volume? True
  M updates consolidated last? False; updates volume? False
  do not treat every close-related flag as M
assertions passed: 18/18
=== E. FINRA 6380A current 10-second off-exchange TRF reporting ===
  10:00 a.m. ET weekday, off-exchange: as soon as practicable but no later than 10 seconds after execution
  8:00 a.m. ET weekday, off-exchange: as soon as practicable but no later than 10 seconds after execution (outside-hours modifier)
  5:00 p.m. ET weekday, off-exchange: as soon as practicable but no later than 10 seconds after execution (outside-hours modifier)
  2:00 a.m. ET weekday, off-exchange: by 4:15 a.m. ET on trade date (not the 10-second clock)
  10:00 p.m. ET weekday, off-exchange: the following business day by 4:15 a.m. ET, designated "as/of"
  Saturday 11:00 a.m. ET, off-exchange: the following business day by 4:15 a.m. ET, designated "as/of"
  10:00 a.m. ET weekday, reported on or through an exchange: not reported to the FINRA/Nasdaq TRF
execution time is reported in hours, minutes and seconds based on Eastern Time
Supplementary Material .02: commence the trade reporting process without delay upon execution;
  in no event may a member purposely withhold trade reports, e.g. by programming systems to delay until the last permissible second
Supplementary Material .05 is a narrow temporary exception for specified qualifying overnight transactions
  (until the earlier of a further TRF-hours amendment's effective date or December 31, 2027); this toy is not that engine
SR-FINRA-2026-015 / 34-105922 / 91 FR 45299 was filed for immediate effectiveness,
  but "The implementation date of the proposed rule change will be the implementation date of the SIP Amendment."
SIP Operating Committees anticipate December 6, 2026; FINRA intends to align, including if that date moves later
after implementation, trades during the new system hours (9:00 p.m. Sunday-8:00 p.m. Friday,
  pause 8:00-9:00 p.m. Monday-Thursday) would be due in 10 seconds, and trades executed while the TRF is closed
  would be due no later than 15 minutes after the TRF opens — those future clocks are not current law
current rulebook selected version is "Mar 30, 2026 - Dec 05, 2026"; "Dec 06, 2026 onwards" is not current law
official May 22 and July 10, 2026 notices: ADF hours are not changing at this time
6380B is the parallel FINRA/NYSE TRF rule; this toy is not a 6380B / ADF / ORF catalog
do not apply 6380A to exchange prints, write that every tape print is delayed by 10 seconds,
  wait until the tenth second on purpose, treat midnight-4:00 a.m. or 8:00 p.m.-midnight prints as already on the 10-second clock,
  or treat December 6, 2026 as an unconditional hard switch
assertions passed: 25/25
disclaimer: official FINRA 6380A current-law clocks; learning only; no venue recommendation
=== F. FINRA 2265: extended hours trading risk disclosure ===
2265(a): No member shall permit a customer to engage in extended hours trading unless the member has furnished
  to the customer, individually, in paper or electronic form, a disclosure statement highlighting
  the risks specific to extended hours trading
official model: "Extended hours trading" means trading outside of “regular trading hours.” “Regular trading hours” generally means
  the time between 9:30 a.m. and 4:00 p.m. Eastern Standard Time
official model wording includes "upon the opening the next morning"
official typography includes "on-line" and "Web site"
official six risks: Lower Liquidity, Higher Volatility, Changing Prices, Unlinked Markets, News Announcements, Wider Spreads
official (b): a member may furnish a substantially similar alternative addressing, at a minimum, the official six risks
official (c): members must consider additional disclosures as necessary
  the model statement is the only permitted text? False
  this toy silently changes "Eastern Standard Time" to ET or EDT? False
  this is a rewrite of already-taught ETH sale-condition T or 6380A? False
no product, broker, or venue recommendation
assertions passed: 28/28
